# Phase 2 — Student, Teacher & Class-Section Management

## Background

Phase 1 has established:
- **Express + Mongoose** server (`server/`) with `User`, `School` models and JWT + RBAC auth
- **React + Vite + Redux** client (`client/`) with `authSlice`, axios interceptors, DashboardLayout, and Tailwind v4
- `sendEmail.js` currently uses **nodemailer** — this will be replaced with **Resend**
- Zod for server-side validation, React Hook Form + Yup on the client
- `ApiResponse` / `ApiError` pattern used across all controllers

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Resend migration**: `sendEmail.js` will be completely rewritten to use `resend` npm package. The `.env` will gain a `RESEND_API_KEY` variable. The existing nodemailer code and `nodemailer` package will be removed.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Multer / Document uploads**: For now, documents are stored in `server/uploads/` (local disk via multer). Cloudinary integration is scaffolded but requires `CLOUDINARY_*` env vars — the code falls back to local storage if they are absent.

> [!WARNING]
> **Mongoose transactions** (Student create) require a **Replica Set** MongoDB connection. The local `mongodb://localhost:27017/school_erp` URI is a standalone instance by default. The code uses `mongoose.startSession()` with a try/catch and graceful fallback comment so dev works without a replica set.

